**Wrong / retracted / deviations.** (1) Codex audit pass 1 found the integer Fourier frequencies were trainable (would have broken periodicity silently) — fixed before any job. (2) **Pre-registration deviated by user decision after the pilot (A4)**: the 5 h/10 h production fits (R=64/128/256, band-limit penalty of A3) were cancelled and the 30-min pilot bank frozen; bar (a) relaxed, bar (b) redefined relative to the floor; "R needed to match POD-64" is unanswered. (3) The autodiff-vs-spectral derivative mismatch was first treated as a correctness issue; it is under-resolution (see above) and the frame never used autodiff. (4) Report audit (Codex) made me qualify the aliasing explanation as an inference, distinguish the registration history, and correct "never computed" vs "cancelled". (5) A stray malformed `submit.sh` call before the test job exited before creating any directory or job (squeue showed exactly one test job).

