### 2026-10-01/02 — quadrature-burgers3d: Hari's off-mesh quadrature on the full-scale Burgers 3D model (lane closed)

**Where.** Worktree `worktrees/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d`, branch `exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d` (forked from `exp/2026-10-01-ns3d-coordnet-bank` @21c175a1b; never pushed; mirrored to `origin/codeonly/exp/2026-10-01-quadrature-burgers3d`). Lane dir `experiments/quadrature-burgers3d/` (DESIGN.md + amendments R1–R5; code offmesh.py, qpanel.py, refjob.py, rules.py, refine_q.py, select_q.py, audit_q.py, npcore.py, make_report.py; vendored frozen model M2 bank sha256 6687f259… and burgers3d-span/retry code). Report `reports/2026-10-01-burgers3d-offmesh-quadrature.md` (generated by make_report.py). Frozen `selection.json` sha256 ca69098a38b4f145178a4612c96bc12d425fe8f53aa47583eef2aaf55e5bf524 (commit 2805fe949, before any held-out job). Namespace `/cluster/tufts/paralab/tawal01/quad3d_20261001/` removed.
**Jobs (10).** smoke1 4731591 (H200; 65-node smoke + 513-node tolerance probe), ref1 4732809 (A100, FAILED GPU preflight, no CUDA device) → ref1 4732869 (H100; 513-node, dt .0025 refined references for 923801×64 and 923901×32), rck1 4733462 (H100; tolerance re-check), val65/129/257 4732813/4732818/4732820 (H200, validation 923801×64), ho65/129/257 4737003/4737005/4737007 (H200, held-out 923901×32). All jax_backend=gpu, f64, highest.
**Setup.** Only the advection term of the frozen R=512 span model is replaced: N^{3/2} Σ w_q ψ(x_q) u (u_x+u_y+u_z)(x_q) with the bank and its analytic (1,1,1)-derivative at the rule points; linear terms, projection and decoding stay mesh-exact; same cached-predictor LM solver (gate G4: identical to the vendor make_fsc). Arms: tensor (incumbent), dense sign-upwind (64³; 4 cases at 128³), CBC lattices 4096/8192/16384/32768, Korobov 16381, Gauss 16³/24³/32³, Sobol 16384; controls lattice-256 and Smolyak level 8. R'∈{512,256}, dt .01.
**Findings (held-out, worst over 32 cases).**
- (i) Lattice beats Gauss at equal m at every mesh/width (continuum ρ, R'=512: 4096 pts 8.3e-2/1.0e-1/1.2e-1 vs Gauss 16³ 0.61–0.62; 32768 pts 0.9–2.0e-4 vs Gauss 32³ 4.7–6.6e-4). Smolyak ρ 24–45, lattice-256 ρ 2–3.4 (both controls fire). A fixed rule's continuum ρ grows with the mesh (sharper reached states): lattice-4096 at R'=512 fails the 0.116 bar at 256³. 4096 lattice points already reach the tensor's refined accuracy everywhere; within 1e-3 of the converged rollout needs 16384 (R'=512, validation) / 4096 (R'=256).
- (ii) Against the 513-node refined reference the off-mesh solve does NOT reproduce the tensor — it is better and mesh-invariant: selected gl24 (R'=512) 2.83 % at 64³/128³/256³ (ratio 1.003; cross-mesh distance 0.072 % → 0.023 %) vs tensor 10.46/6.09/3.87 % (ratio 2.70; 4.6 % → 2.8 %); lat4096 (R'=256) 4.49 % at all meshes vs tensor 10.57/6.56/5.07 %. The tensor tracks the same-mesh FOM's first-order upwind error (best FOM refined 9.85/5.22/2.27 %). Off-mesh vs tensor distance = the O(h) gap (ρ of dense upwind vs continuum 0.195/0.098/0.052). At 64³/128³ no same-mesh FOM setting is as accurate as the off-mesh solve; at 256³ the best FOM (2.27 %) is.
- (iii) Cost: off-mesh query cheaper than the tensor in all six cells (R'=512: 34.1 vs 47.9, 40.6 vs 52.0, 76.7 vs 90.1 ms; R'=256: 11.1 vs 12.2, 12.1 vs 14.1, 33.0 vs 35.1 ms). Memory 0.34 GB (gl24) / 50 MB (lat4096) vs 4.30 GB / 0.54 GB tensor; Jacobian 0.66 vs 1.04 ms despite 29 vs 1.1 GFLOP (GEMM vs bandwidth-bound contraction). At 256³ query time is dominated by mesh projection/decoding. Speedups vs Newton–BiCGStab at 256³: same-grid rule 2.21×→2.59× (R'512), 5.66×→6.01× (R'256); refined rule 2.21×→6.45× (R'512). At 64³ every reduced arm is slower than the FOM. Same-job tensor reproduces the published 256³ row (2.20 %/2.21×, 3.77 %/5.66×).
- (iv) k-head not revisited; nothing retrained.
**Gates/audits.** G1–G4, table, reference, continuum-target check (≤1.2e-7) pass at every panel; timing gates pass (ROM neighbour check untested at 256³: no arm 4× slower than another). NumPy audits pass on all six panels (refined errors in-job vs NumPy ≤2.8e-16; every recorded worst ρ reproduced; fault injections detected). Codex: design audit (4 blockers, fixed in R1), R1 re-check (fixed in R2), results audit (no blockers; majors fixed in the report).
**Wrong / retracted / deviations.** (1) Design audit: vendor FOM would stack all 100 states at 513 nodes (~107 GB) and capture the spectral array; replaced by a lean FOM (gate: identical to vendor at 65 nodes). Selection had an unconditional fallback — removed. (2) ref1 4732809 failed the GPU preflight; restaged unchanged on H100. (3) The smoke probe could not discriminate reference tolerances; R4 re-check found up to 1.02e-5 (one of four cases above the 1e-5 threshold) → reference declared tolerance-limited at ~1e-5 (refined differences <1.0e-4 unresolved; immaterial at the %-level differences reported). (4) Smoke panel timing gates failed (2 cases × 2 reps; diagnostic only). (5) Held-out audits first run with the held-out re-selection check, which "failed" because re-applying the rule to held-out data picks lat8192 instead of the frozen gl24 at R'=512 (lat8192 missed the 1e-3 rollout criterion on validation by 0.02–0.03 pp); that is a stability finding, not an audit failure — audits re-run without it (originals kept in results/superseded/). (6) Richardson estimate u_R = 2u_513 − u_257 added post-hoc after validation (R5), diagnostic only; refined reference itself differs from u_R by up to 2.28 %. (7) Codex results audit: report had a wrong median (47.7→47.1 s), an overstated "all certified rules agree" claim, and an ambiguous speedup sentence — fixed. (8) Held-out cohort 923901 had been evaluated before by the retry lane for its tensor settings (disclosed).
